# LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The codebase already treats LF as an invariant — brainspaces.py seeds Brain files
# with newline="\n", and test_brainspaces.py asserts the result carries no CRLF — but
# without this file a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the runner default) hands
# back the packaged templates with CRLF. Anything comparing a seeded file against its
# packaged source then fails on Windows only, which is a slow bug to find.
#
# Shell scripts must be LF to run at all; the hook writes bytes straight to stdout and
# counts them against a payload limit, so line endings there change a measured size.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
